        "marks": 1
       },
       {
        "id": "p2",
        "description": "A1 converts to index form: $\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{y}} = 3^2 = 9$, so $x = 9\\sqrt{y}$.",
        "marks": 1
       }
      ]
     },
     "modelAnswer": "$$\n\\log_3 x - \\frac{1}{2}\\log_3 y = 2 \\Rightarrow \\log_3 x - \\log_3 \\sqrt{y} = 2\n$$\n\n$$\n\\log_3 \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{y}} = 2 \\Rightarrow \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{y}} = 9 \\Rightarrow x = 9\\sqrt{y}\n$$"
    },
    "explanation": "Power law, quotient law, then index form."
   },
   {
    "label": "(c)",
    "type": "NUMERICAL",
    "marks": 3,
    "stem": "Use $xy = 243$ to find the value of $y$.",
