    },
    "explanation": "$9\\sqrt{y} \\times y = 243$, so $y^{\\frac{3}{2}} = 27$ and $y = 27^{\\frac{2}{3}} = 9$.",
    "workedSolution": "1. $9\\sqrt{y} \\times y = 243$, so $y^{\\frac{3}{2}} = 27$ and $y = 27^{\\frac{2}{3}} = 9$."
   },
   {
    "label": "(d)",
    "type": "NUMERICAL",
    "marks": 1,
